{
 "title": "Delhi (UT) road accidents by time of day, road classification and place of occurrence, NCRB Accidental Deaths and Suicides in India, 2014 to 2022",
 "status": "staged",
 "scope": "The DELHI (UT) row of NCRB ADSI Tables 1A.2, 1A.6, 1A.7 and 1A.11 for each year. Road accidents only. Not the Delhi (City) row, and the railway and railway-crossing columns are not read. These are NCRB counts from the returns sent to it, not the Traffic Police statistics, and the two differ in some years (see README).",
 "how_read": "Time of day and road classification were read from the rendered page images and also taken from the PDF text by position; the two readings agree for every year. Place of occurrence was taken from the PDF text by position. Every row is checked: time bands add to the printed total, road classes add to the printed total for cases, injured and died, case totals equal the 1A.2 and the time-of-day totals, place categories add to the printed rural and urban subtotals and to the grand total, and the grand total equals the road-classification deaths. The tests repeat these checks.",
 "definitions": {
  "time_of_day": "Accidents (cases), by the three-hour band in which they occurred.",
  "road_classification": "Accidents (cases), persons injured and persons died, by the class of road. An expressways column is used from 2015.",
  "place_of_death": "Persons died, by place of occurrence, split rural and urban and by sex. Delhi reports almost all of its deaths as urban."
 },
